# No Magic Strings (HARD FAIL)

This is a **blocking** project law. Violations fail the change — do not ship and do not ask to waive.

Full policy: `artifacts/coding-standards/CURRENT/magic-string-policy.md` + `constants-policy.md`.

## Before every edit / PR

1. Search the touch set for product literals (routes, statuses, types, roles, currencies, error codes, storage/query keys, locales, themes, cookies).
2. If a constant exists → **import and use it**. Never re-type the literal.
3. If it does not exist → **add it once** at the documented home, then import.
4. Comparisons, `switch`, Zod `z.enum`, defaults, and UI option arrays are all call sites — same rule.

## Constant homes (extend; do not invent a 4th)

| Scope | Path |
|-------|------|
| Routes / path builders | `modules/tenancy/application/app-path.ts` (`APP_PATH`, `moneyTransactionPath`, …) |
| Auth / tenancy | `modules/tenancy/application/*-constants.ts`, `product-action-error.ts` |
| Ledger | `modules/ledger/application/ledger-constants.ts` |
| Plan | `modules/plan/application/plan-constants.ts` |
| Inbox | `modules/inbox/application/inbox-constants.ts` |
| App-wide keys/config | `shared/constants/`, `shared/config/` |

## Shape (required)

```ts
export const TransactionDirection = {
  INCOME: "income",
  EXPENSE: "expense",
} as const;

export type TransactionDirection =
  (typeof TransactionDirection)[keyof typeof TransactionDirection];

export const TRANSACTION_DIRECTION_VALUES = [
  TransactionDirection.INCOME,
  TransactionDirection.EXPENSE,
] as const;

// Zod must share the same source:
z.enum(TRANSACTION_DIRECTION_VALUES)
```

Re-export values from barrels with `export { X }` only (merged const+type). Do **not** also `export type { X }` for the same name.

## Forbidden (examples)

```ts
// ❌
href={`/money/transactions/${id}`}
listCategoryTags("expense")
z.enum(["income", "expense"])
status === "pending"
currency ?? "VND"
;(["expense", "income"] as const).map(...)

// ✅
href={moneyTransactionPath(id)}
listCategoryTags(TransactionDirection.EXPENSE)
z.enum(TRANSACTION_DIRECTION_VALUES)
status === InboxItemStatus.PENDING
currency ?? DEFAULT_CURRENCY
TRANSACTION_DIRECTION_OPTIONS.map(...)
```

## Allowed exceptions only

- `t("…")` message keys and `data-testid` values
- One-off strings with **no** product meaning and **no** reuse
- Test fixtures may assert via the **constant** (`expect(x).toBe(TransactionDirection.EXPENSE)`), never a fresh literal that duplicates a domain constant

## Self-check (must pass before finishing)

- [ ] No new hardcoded route / status / type / role / currency / error-code / key literal at a call site
- [ ] New domain values added to the correct `*-constants.ts` (or shared home) first
- [ ] Zod / UI option lists import the same `*_VALUES` / `*_OPTIONS` arrays
